{"availability":"available","full":"jtwalters25/intent-engine","name":"intent-engine","description":"Deterministic, explainable intent-aware re-ranking. Same catalog, different intent, different order,  across streaming, music, e-commerce, ride matching, and food delivery.","category":"Business","language":"Python","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2026-02-08T03:29:29Z","updated":"2026-10-08T18:46:40Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://dist-pied-one-60.vercel.app","topics":[],"demo":"https://intentengine.vercel.app/demo","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T23:43:28.902Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T23:43:28.902Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T23:43:28.902Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T23:43:28.902Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A deterministic, intent-aware re-ranking engine with a React prototype UI. It shows how contextual intent signals (time of day, viewer profile, energy level, device) can reshape content recommendations without ML, personalization, or randomness.","Prototype. Built to demonstrate systems thinking and backend architecture, not a production service.","As a parent, I spend real time every day filtering kids' content by hand, because streaming recommendations optimize for engagement rather than the intent I have in the moment (\"it's bedtime,\" \"keep it calm\"). My take as an engineer is that this belongs in a deterministic, explainable re-ranking layer instead of a model you can't inspect: the same context should always produce the same, traceable ordering, and every score should break down into signals a person can read. This repo is where I test that idea across more than one domain."],"features":["Honest status per vertical. Functional means it has a real catalog, 4 context presets, and 5 signal sliders that drive deterministic client-side scoring. All five verticals are functional in the demo; none are UI-only…","No vertical is UI-only or a pl